B.a70={chart:0,cellarbook:1,ovenlog:2,extension:3,watch:4,clock:5,phone:6,souffle:7,boots:8,scoresheet:9,loafstand:10,planner:11,mudprint:12,seedglaze:13,loafdirt:14,loafkennel:15,deed:16,signboard:17,latchbook:18,prints:19}
B.a5s=new A.ar(B.a70,["Splendid. Now all we want is the weapon.",u.h,u.S,u.X,u.Q,u.Q,u.B,"I believe in that pudding, Churlock. She was at that oven all hour. But notice what else is in that kitchen, six feet from the oven.","Read whose handwriting that is, old chap. We have one dessert's word for when that door was opened, and no more.","No gaps, and each man watching the other. Those two were in the parlor till midnight. I wonder what they heard at midnight.","Kept in Penny's pantry. Whoever took it either lives in that kitchen or walked through it.","Every servant in this house was to lose their place. That is a motive for three of them. We want something narrower.","Garden clay, on top of the custard, wet. And yet the gardener was locked out of doors until midnight. Who says so?","On top of the custard, so after she fell. And yet the only tart in the house was locked out until midnight. Who says so?",u.m,u.m,"Two names on one piece of paper, Churlock. And a sum neither of them could find by the month end.","Two names on one piece of board, Churlock. And a sum neither of them could find by the month end.","Read it from top to bottom, old chap, as it was written. In the order it was written.",u.A],t.w)
B.Vu=s(["Every one of the five has an alibi this time, Churlock, and I believe four of them. So look for the alibi that is true and still does not matter.","Barry was locked out until midnight. Who told us so? One dessert, in her own handwriting. Now ask the rest of the house what they heard at midnight, and what the dog did.","The weapon came from the pantry and ended up in the yard. To do either, you must pass through the kitchen. Who was in the kitchen, and what did she say she saw?","She never left her oven, old chap, and she never had to. A bolt can be drawn in ten seconds. Read the latch book again, line by line, and then name the one who opened the door and the one who came through it."],t.s)
B.aup=new A.f("what","What happened to her?","Victim is Mrs. \xc9claire Senclair, founder of Senclair Confections. One blow from above, Detective, with something hard and heavy that comes to a blunt point. Cracked her shell like an egg. We traced where she fell in powdered sugar.",B.b,B.b,null)
B.atc=new A.f("weapon","What was the weapon?","Couldn't tell you. Shaped like a cone, weighs as much as a brick, and it isn't down here. Whoever swung it took it away with them.",B.b,B.b,null)
B.VU=s([B.aup,B.atc,B.eD,B.de],t.q)
B.a0H=s(["mudprint","seedglaze"],t.s)
B.aw2=new A.f("tread","Could that mark have been made this morning?","Not a chance. Nobody has been within a yard of that outline since we chalked it but me and the Sarge, and we kept the gardener shut in the boiler room till you came. It was there when we arrived.",B.a0H,B.b,null)
B.a2x=s([B.iP,B.iS,B.iK,B.iM,B.iJ,B.aw2],t.q)
B.awL=new A.f("about","Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","Strict, but fair, I always said. She paid on time. Thirty years I cooked for that woman, Detective, and I'd have cooked thirty more.",B.b,B.b,null)
B.a0r=s(["loafstand"],t.s)
B.ata=new A.f("loaf","Your sugarloaf is missing.","My sugarloaf! It was on its stand at supper, in its blue paper. I nipped a piece off for the souffl\xe9 at ten and wrapped it up again. Somebody's had it out of my pantry.",B.a0r,B.b,null)
B.a0q=s(["loafdirt","loafkennel"],t.s)
B.arE=new A.f("yard","The sugarloaf was hidden out in the yard.","In the yard? Well, nobody went out through my kitchen while I was basting, I can promise you that. It must have been carried out after half eleven, when I'd gone up.",B.a0q,B.b,null)
B.Z3=s(["boots"],t.s)
B.Pv=new A.r("latchbook","Night-Latch Book","",0,"Last night's page of the latch book, three entries, one under another. \u201c10:00. All doors latched. G.C.\u201d Then, in Penny's hand: \u201c12:00. Let Barry in from the greenhouse. P.C.\u201d And below that, also hers: \u201c11:30. Souffl\xe9 out, oven banked, kitchen lamps down. P.C.\u201d",B.aR,B.u,null,B.f,B.b,!1,"penny")
B.arR=new A.f("book","May I see the night-latch book?","The latch book? It hangs by the front door. Here's last night's page. Graham latches up and signs, and I sign for anyone I let in after. It's all in order.",B.Z3,B.b,B.Pv)
B.a0l=s(["latchbook"],t.s)
B.auF=new A.f("order","You wrote midnight above half past eleven.","Did I? I... I'll have left a line and gone back to fill it in. I was all of a wobble, Detective. I'm all of a wobble now.",B.a0l,B.b,null)
B.awb=new A.f("prints","Your fingerprints are on the sugarloaf.","It's my sugar, Detective. I nip it every day of my life. You'd find my fingerprints on every loaf in Donut County.",B.aa,B.b,null)
B.aw6=new A.f("carried","Barry says he carried the sugar in for you.","He did, bless him. Tuesday. It's a weight, a full loaf, and my wrists aren't what they were.",B.b,B.nC,null)
B.tH=s(["deed","signboard"],t.s)
B.avy=new A.f("teagarden","You and Barry have paid a deposit on a tea garden.","It's a daydream, Detective, that's all. An old woman and a gardener and a pot of tea. We'd never have found the balance. ...We'd never have found it.",B.tH,B.b,null)
B.nA=s(["planner"],t.s)
B.av4=new A.f("sale","She was selling the company, and your recipe with it.","Selling? She never said one word to me. Not one. I'd no idea until this minute.",B.nA,B.b,null)
B.UP=s([B.dz,B.awL,B.l6,B.ata,B.arE,B.arR,B.auF,B.awb,B.aw6,B.avy,B.av4,B.eC,B.dq,B.eQ,B.dy,B.dx,B.dB,B.ds,B.dk,B.dG,B.dA],t.q)
B.p3=new A.f("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","In the parlor, sir, at chess with the Colonel, from half past ten until two minutes to midnight. Neither of us left the board.",B.b,B.b,null)
B.FL=new A.f("eleven","Why was she in the cellar at eleven at night?","Madam locked the wine rack herself at eleven each night, sir, and took the key to bed. She had done so for thirty years. Everybody under this roof could set a watch by it.",B.b,B.b,null)
B.a38=s(["penny/letin"],t.s)
B.asP=new A.f("dog","Did you hear Penny let Barry in at midnight?","I did not, sir, though the Colonel and I were in the parlor until two minutes to, and I was in the hall directly after. I will say this: the dog barks whenever that back door is opened after dark. One hears it all over the house.",B.b,B.a38,null)
B.auw=new A.f("delivery","Barry says he carried the sugar in on Tuesday.","The grocer delivers on Thursdays, sir, at four. I signed for one sugarloaf yesterday afternoon and carried it to the pantry myself. The gardener was not in the house, and Mrs. Cotta was at the market.",B.b,B.nC,null)
B.auo=new A.f("sale","She was selling the company and dismissing the staff.","I had gathered as much, sir. I have my savings and a sister in Shortbread. It would have been an inconvenience. It was not a catastrophe.",B.nA,B.b,null)
