B.a5e=new A.ar(B.a6L,[u.Q,u.Q,"Splendid. Now all we want is the weapon.",u.F,u.C,u.S,u.o,"A handle at either end, old chap. Could one dessert carry that down a flight of steps? Dust it, and then ask the foreman who moves the barrels.","A machine that counts, at a rate written on its own side. Do the sum, Churlock.",u._,"Saturday, and two sets of initials. Somebody's Saturday was going to be very unpleasant.","A belt, to a windmill that never stops. A machine can be cranked by a hand, Churlock, or by the weather.","Hard as glass. Marsha knows taffy. I should ask her what makes it go like that.","When we are free. Free of what, I wonder, or of whom?","Two names in one letter, and both of them losing everything by Sunday.","Two traces, one at each end. Marsha knows every dessert on this farm. Ask her.","Two trails, side by side. Marsha knows every dessert on this farm, and their feet. Ask her.","Do the sum, old chap. Pulls, minutes, and what the plate on the machine says a hand can manage.",u.u],t.w)
B.a_M=s([u.H,"Three of them are placed by a pie, a creamery slip and a railway ticket. The other two are placed only by each other, and a machine.","Go down to the press shed and look hard at the puller, at what is joined to it, and at what came out of it.","A barrel with a handle at either end, and a hand on each. And a tally of pulls that no hand could crank. Name them both."],t.s)
B.att=new A.f("what","What happened to him?","Victim's Cornelius Kernel, the candy corn king. A barrel of rock candy came down the cellar steps and went right over him. We traced where he lay in icing sugar.",B.b,B.b,null)
B.arp=new A.f("weapon","Could it have been an accident?","That barrel lives in the corner behind the potatoes, Detective. Somebody carried it to the top of those steps first, and it's no one-man job. Work it out.",B.b,B.b,null)
