B.a5S=new A.dp("fpull","Pulled Together",B.ajM,B.ZF,B.UI,B.eb,10,B.aka,B.OL,B.tN,"1868",B.a5e,B.a_M,B.ai,B.bf,B.ai,B.a5g,"Lolly Popwell and Taffy Pulman were secretly engaged, and Farmer Kernel had found out. He meant to dismiss Taffy on Saturday and swore his daughter would never marry a farmhand while he lived. They said they spent the evening together in the press shed, Taffy cranking the puller while Lolly watched. But at twenty to eleven Taffy belted the puller to the windmill shaft, and it cranked itself, faster than any hand could, all night. Together they carried a barrel of rock candy to the top of the cellar steps and at 11:05 rolled it down onto the farmer. The tally Taffy produced counts 3,412 pulls in an hour, on a machine whose own brass plate says no hand can do more than twenty a minute. And the taffy came out hard as glass, because no hand had warmed it. Marsha was at her pie, Gus at the barn door with the creamery man, and the Professor on the last train home.",B.a_A)
