B.a5P=new A.dp("fcream","The Cream of the Crop",B.akk,B.Vf,B.Zu,B.eb,10,B.ak5,B.OP,B.u9,"1880",B.a5u,B.YB,B.ai,B.bf,B.ai,B.a5j,"Forty years ago Gus Gumdrop's father staked the Gumdrop farm on a hand of cards, and lost it to Cornelius Kernel. Gus had worked the land that should have been his for twenty-two years, and on Sunday he learned that the farmer was selling it to Big Sugar and letting him go. His alibi was the creamery slip that said he handed over the churns at the barn door at eleven. But the driver never comes to the barn: he takes the churns from the stand at the gate at half past ten, and writes eleven on every slip from habit. Gus left the churns out early, went down to the root cellar, and at 11:05 struck the farmer with a full iron milk churn. The cows were never milked at all, and bellowed all night. The milking card he produced lists Fudge Ripple, a cow sold to the Nougat farm on the first of the month. Marsha was at her pie, Lolly on the telephone, Taffy at the puller, and the Professor on the last train home.",B.a27)
