B.a5Q=new A.dp("fslice","A Slice Too Many",B.akd,B.Xn,B.Tw,B.eb,10,B.ajS,B.PD,B.a0B,"1874",B.a4O,B.Yt,B.ai,B.bf,B.ai,B.a5h,"Marsha Mallow and Professor Licorice had sold the Kernel candy corn recipe and seed to Big Sugar, half each, and Farmer Kernel had found the letters. The Professor never took the last train: he came home early and kept to his room, and his ticket was never punched. At five to eleven Marsha left her pie and took the farmer down to the root cellar for a look at the corn, and at 11:05 the Professor struck him with her iron skillet. Her pie went a quarter of an hour unturned and burnt black on one side, and two slices were gone from it by midnight. The bake card she produced has the Professor coming in off the last train at twenty past eleven, when the timetable on the porch has that train leaving Candy City at that very minute. Lolly was on the telephone, Taffy at the puller, and Gus at the barn door with the creamery man.",B.tN)
