B.a5K=new A.dp("fchute","Down the Chute",B.ak2,B.Vg,B.XY,B.eb,10,B.ajK,B.PA,B.u9,"1876",B.a55,B.XJ,B.ai,B.bf,B.ai,B.a5l,"The farm's pension fund passed, on Farmer Kernel's death, to his two longest-serving hands: Gus Gumdrop and Marsha Mallow. On Friday he meant to dissolve it. Neither of them went near the root cellar. At five to eleven Marsha sent the farmer down with a note, to fetch up a sack of potatoes for a pie that has no potatoes in it, and stood him under the mouth of the corn chute. Gus handed his churns to the creamery man at eleven, unlocked the chute with the key Marsha had been keeping for him, and at 11:05 pulled the lever. A ton of candy corn came down on the farmer. Both alibis were true. The barn log Gus produced says the chute was padlocked and the only key on his belt, but the key was in Marsha's recipe box. Lolly was on the telephone, Taffy at the puller, and the Professor on the last train home.",B.a0v)
