B.a5M=new A.dp("fline","On the Line",B.ajY,B.Wv,B.Ur,B.eb,10,B.ajJ,B.OH,B.a0C,"1883",B.a4J,B.U_,B.ai,B.bf,B.ai,B.a5m,"Farmer Kernel had written a new will leaving the farm to the Candy Land Agricultural Society, and had torn up the Talent Bureau's offer to his daughter with \u201cOVER MY DEAD BODY\u201d across it. Lolly Popwell's alibi was the telephone: an audition down the line from ten to eleven till half past, and the exchange swears the line never dropped. But she had spliced forty feet of Gus's barn cable into the telephone cord, and carried the receiver down to the top of the cellar steps, singing. At four minutes past eleven she set it down, struck her father with the brass doorstop from the front door, and was back on the line two minutes later, out of breath. The Bureau marked her down for it. The letter she produced, saying she sang without a single pause, is in her own pink ink. Marsha was at her pie, Gus at the barn door, Taffy at the puller, and the Professor on the last train home.",B.a0A)
