B.a5N=new A.dp("fcrank","No Crank",B.akh,B.a2D,B.Vc,B.eb,10,B.akb,B.P0,B.a_B,"1886",B.a58,B.Wg,B.ai,B.bf,B.ai,B.a5i,"For three summers Taffy Pulman had been pulling taffy from Kernel sugar on Kernel time and selling it at the county fair under his own name, and on Friday the farmer meant to fetch the police. Taffy's alibi was the puller's counter: 1,190 pulls, a fair hour's cranking. But he cranked that batch at eight o'clock, not at eleven, and left it on the slab, where it went cold and gathered dust. At eleven he took the iron crank handle off the machine, went down to the root cellar, and at 11:05 struck the farmer with it. Without its handle the puller could not be turned at all, and that night, for the first time in years, it never squealed. His tally card has the batch warm as toast at midnight. Marsha was at her pie, Gus at the barn door, Lolly on the telephone, and the Professor on the last train home.",B.a0u)
